.TH "CSDLC-REBUILD" "1" "September 11, 2026" "C-SDLC v3" "ADL Operator Manual"
.SH NAME
csdlc\-rebuild \- explicitly rebuild all six cards from the semantic issue record
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\&csdlc rebuild ISSUE [\-\-repo\-root ROOT] [\-\-json]
\&csdlc rebuild ISSUE \-\-emit\-request
\&csdlc rebuild \-\-intent\-request REQUEST.json
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
\&Semantic issue intent forms are the current operational contract. Rebuild resolves the authenticated issue, bound checkout, active prompt registry and exact semantic source version before any write.
.PP
\&Derive all six SIP, STP, SPP, VPP, SRP and SOR values and rendered cards from the single semantic issue record. Write projection artifacts deterministically and publish the manifest last, then acknowledge that exact projection through the transaction owner.
.PP
\&Status and validate report healthy, missing, altered or interrupted projection state without writing. Rebuild is the explicit repair operation. An unchanged healthy projection is an expected no\-op with identical bytes and digests.
.PP
\&Rebuild preserves semantic facts, evidence references and immutable receipt bytes. It cannot create approval, proof, accepted review findings, publication or terminal completion. Pending work, stale semantic identity, corrupted retained state and mismatched issue or checkout fail closed.
.PP
\&The generated wrapper emitted by \-\-emit\-request can be passed directly to \-\-intent\-request; its semantic_version prevents a reviewed request from silently rebuilding a later semantic record.
.SH OUTPUT
\&Machine JSON uses the common command\-result envelope and reports projection health, semantic digest, projection digest, generated paths, mutation truth and semantic version.
.SH RECOVERY
\&If projection writing is interrupted, retain the pending marker and staged artifacts. Ordinary inspection remains read\-only. Use the explicit recover route and exact preview digest; do not bless or hand\-edit partial output.
.SH SEE ALSO
\&csdlc(1), csdlc\-status(1), csdlc\-validate(1), csdlc\-recover(1), csdlc\-workflow(1), docs/csdlc\-v3/INTENT_COMMANDS.md.
.SH OPTIONS
\&Supported intent options: \-\-emit\-request, \-\-help, \-\-intent\-request, \-\-json, \-\-repo\-root, \-h. Positional ISSUE is positive; unsupported content, preview and execute arguments fail closed.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
\&csdlc status ISSUE
\&csdlc rebuild ISSUE
\&csdlc validate ISSUE
.fi
.PP
\&Use an isolated selected candidate for qualification. This operation does not authorize live conversion, writer activation or shared binary replacement.
